# CREDITS — The Crossing

A 40-second film in the Risograph Print style, made entirely in code.
The harbour, the two boats and the story are invented. No real brand, place or person is portrayed.

## Voice
Speech synthesis: Kokoro (kokoro-onnx), voice `af_heart`, English, offline.
Model and engine follow the licences of the kokoro-onnx project
(https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx).

## Music
Original score, written for this film (`music/score.py`).
Upright bass, nylon guitar and toy piano are physically modelled
(`core/audio/pluck.py`). The marimba is synthesised in the same score.

## Typefaces
- Cormorant Garamond — SIL Open Font License 1.1 (Catharsis Fonts). See `fonts/OFL.txt`.
  The files are the same OFL build used by the Impasto demo in this repository.

## Picture
Every frame is drawn by this film's plate engine (`draw.js`, `scene.js`) and
printed by its shader (`riso.js`). No stock footage, photographs or third-party images.

## Sound effects
All foley is synthesised for this film (`mix.py`): water, motors, paper feed,
drum hits, a buoy, a sheet landing and a pin.
